      "source_url": "https://cdn.clinicaltrials.gov/large-docs/16/NCT04237116/Prot_000.pdf",
      "source_excerpt": "Protocol sections 4.2, 6.1.4 and 8; Table 8-1 Assessment schedule: \"This study consists of a Screening Period (up\" \"to 4 weeks) and 2 Treatment Periods (covering 24 weeks in total).\" \"Treatment period 1\" \"Treatment period 2\" \"Starting from Week 12, all patients will receive secukinumab 300 mg s.c.\" \"Patients who were randomized to placebo during Treatment Period 1 will\" \"Patients who were randomized to secukinumab during Treatment Period 1 will\" \"The 12-week placebo-controlled Treatment Period 1 will allow indirect comparisons to\" \"primary endpoint at Week 12 and assessment of effects on NAFLD related endpoints\" \"placebo will switch to active treatment with secukinumab 300 mg for Treatment Period 2\" \"(Week 12 up to Week 20).\" \"This is a 24-week study.\" \"Patients will receive either secukinumab or placebo (2:1 ratio) for the\" \"first 12 weeks of the study (last study drug injection at Week 8), then secukinumab or\" \"randomized to receive secukinumab during Treatment Period 1) for the next 12 weeks of the\" \"study (last study drug injection at Week 20).\" \"The Assessment Schedule (Table 8-1) lists all of the assessments when they are performed.\" \"discontinue during Treatment Period 1 and EOT2 (Week 24) for patients who prematurely\" \"discontinue during Treatment Period 2.\" \"safety evaluations during the 4 weeks following the last dose of study treatment, including\" \"CAIN457ADE15\" \"Screening§ Baseline Treatment Period 1 Treatment Period 2\" \"Week (relative to baseline) -4 to -1 BSL 1 2 3 4 8 12 13 14 15 16 20 24 Uns§§\" \"Day -28 to -7 1 8 15 22 29 57 85 92 99 106 113 141 169\" \"Patient’s eligibility for the study will be assessed during Screening period (Day -28 to -7)\" \"including Screening Visit 1, Screening Visit 2 and at the Baseline Visit (see Table 8-1).\" \"The primary endpoint variable is the PASI90 response at Week 12.\" \"The first study treatment administration will occur at the Baseline Visit, after all study\" -- The protocol states a screening period up to four weeks and two treatment periods covering 24 weeks; the first treatment period begins at baseline (the protocol identifies the first administration as occurring at the Baseline Visit) and ends at Week 12 and the second at Week 24. The protocol calls this a 24-week study and identifies the primary PASI90 endpoint at Week 12. Table 8-1 gives the scheduled post-baseline visits and days and confirms the full visit schedule is present in this cited file. Week 24 is the end of the planned treatment period and final scheduled visit; Week 20 is the last planned injection. The separate four-week safety contact requirement applies after early treatment discontinuation, so it is not represented as planned follow-up. Screening duration is left null because it is stated as 'up to' four weeks, not fixed. End-of-study week is recorded as Week 24 relative to baseline, which is the first-dose baseline visit.",
